---
description: Keep universal algorithms free of project-specific parameter/domain logic
alwaysApply: true
---

# No project logic in universal algorithms

Do not hardcode project-specific parameter names, domains, or special cases inside shared/universal code paths (e.g. `SettingsNavigator` get/save formatting, generic parsers, template processors).

**Not allowed:** branching in a reusable algorithm on concrete project keys or units.

```cpp
// BAD — universal formatter knows project parameter names
if (paramName == "pressure>sensorMinVolts" || paramName == "pressure>sensorMaxVolts") {
    return String(value, 3);
}
return String(value, 2);
```

**Allowed:** express project needs as data/config on the descriptor or registration site; the algorithm stays generic.

```cpp
// GOOD — metadata on ParamDescriptor; algorithm uses it for any FLOAT
return String(value, descriptor->decimalPlaces);

// GOOD — project-specific choice only at registration
new ParamDescriptor("pressure>sensorMinVolts", FLOAT, ..., 3);
```

Same idea elsewhere: extend the shared type/API with a neutral field or hook; configure it where project settings are declared. Do not grow `if (name == "...")` lists inside the shared path.
